--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the size of the array), then for every index j greater than the given index and less than the previous size of the array minus one, the element at index j is either null and the next element was also null, or the element at index j is equal to the next element before the removal.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the size of the array), then for every index greater than the specified index and less than the old size minus one, either both the current and the next elements are null, or the current element is equal to the next old element.
